ignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\n24:## 1. Problem statement and repository baseline\n26:### 1.1 Current repository baseline\n48:### 1.2 Three problems to solve together\n56:## 2. Derivation from foundations and non-negotiable invariants\n60:### 2.1 Foundational axioms & three-tier hybrid rationale\n74:### 2.1a Alignment with the tao architecture's second axiom (`yang.tao.md` §2.2)\n84:### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\n103:## 3. Three-tier hybrid architecture & prelude layering\n134:### 3.1 Litmus test: Native Host `:pure` vs. Guest `%capture` Effects vs. VM Effects\n142:### 3.2 Explicit exclusions from Layer 2a (`yrt.*`)\n156:## 4. Host `:pure` core extensions & Layer 2a (`yrt.*`) specifications\n158:### 4.1 Native host `:pure` core extensions (`data`, `float`, `kind`)\n185:### 4.2 `yang.call` *(existing Layer-2a leaf)*\n189:### 4.3 `yrt.effect` — Unified guest algebraic effects over `%capture`\n231:### 4.4 `yrt.int` — Exact-integer adapters and radix scanners\n242:### 4.5 `yrt.safepoint` *(Track B — deferred)*\n248:## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\n252:### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\n301:### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n314:## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n316:### 6.1 Focused profile scope: Yin/Clojure DEFAULT + Native legacy track\n325:### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n336:### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n468:### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\n483:### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n493:## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n495:### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\n514:### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `:pure` host core + `yrt.effect`)\n535:### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n554:### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n569:### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n574:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n589:### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n607:## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n609:### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n616:### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n634:### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden discipline (Clean-Slate)\n640:## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n647:| **P1′ — `yrt.effect` + `yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers; unified trusted `clj`** | Implement stateless `yrt.effect` (5-slot `data/nth` frames, abortive `raise`/`try-value`/`try-orelse`/`try-finally`/`call-ec`, plus resumable `handle`/`perform` — the frame design anticipates py/php `:depth` accounting but only clj/clj.py exercise it) and `yrt.int`; upgrade `clj` to the unified trusted form (two-step `make-callable`, evaluated `assoc` conditions, `invoke-callable`, `prim-get`/`prim-assoc`, retiring `yang.clojure`'s `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance ops); add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`. **py/js/php preludes untouched** — they keep their own mechanisms. | Refresh `clj`/`yang.clojure` goldens cleanly; py/js/php goldens untouched | `yrt.effect` unit tests (abortive, `finally`, resumable one-shot `handle`/`perform`, cold policy traps) across semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity under shadowed `(defn get ...)`; clj-only synthetic nonzero depth/base fixtures exercising the `:depth` slot; independent concurrent `clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. (H7 repair: native collection invocation — including the landed fixture where a locally bound map invoked with `:k` returns 9, which requires the native data-call dispatch to admit locally bound maps — and bundled primitive shadowing through the new standard library gate in the P2′ row below; the REAL cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind with cleanup and context restoration gates SOLELY in the P3′ row.) |\n648:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store before VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py` exists. |\n655:## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:71:(defn compile-program-and-run\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:83:(deftest test-compile-literals\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:107:(deftest test-set-lite