{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/clojure/donor_link_test.clj\nsed -n '1,112p;165,240p' test/yang/call/conformance.clj\nsed -n '850,882p;1105,1125p;1788,1820p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nrg -n 'defn handle|\\\\[yrt.effect/(handle|perform)' src/cljc/yang/rt/effect.cljc\nrg -n 'def \\\\\"'^:private (av|outcome)-modules|register-data-module|register-cell-module'\"' test/yang/clojure_test.clj\nrg -n 'data/(append|str-length|char-at|normalize-key)|canonical-entries' src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.clojure.donor-link-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [yang.clojure :as clj]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.core.module :as module]\n            [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yang.rt.effect :as effect]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]))\n\n\n(deftest linked-donor-uses-runtime-context\n  (let [{:keys [store call-address]} @h/published\n        registry (prelude/admit (h/registry))\n        effect-address (:address (h/publish-guest-module! (effect/module-spec registry)))\n        runtime (h/publish-guest-module! (prelude/module-spec registry call-address effect-address))\n        unit (clj/lower-unit '[(defn f [x] (try (throw x) (catch Exception e e)))\n                               (f 42)])\n        ast (u/annotate-call-sites\n              (module/module-tree [(module/require-node 'clj) (u/def! 'body unit)]))\n        spec (module/module-spec :test/refusal :test/undeclared registry\n                                 {:name 'test.clj-donor :ast ast :exports '#{body}\n                                  :runtime-name 'clj :runtime-address (:address runtime)\n                                  :deps {'yang.call call-address}})\n        donor (h/publish-guest-module! spec)\n        caller-ast (u/annotate-call-sites\n                     (module/module-tree\n                       [(module/require-node 'clj)\n                        (module/require-node 'test.clj-donor)\n                        (u/def! 'run (u/sexp->uast\n                                       '(fn [] (clj/run-main test.clj-donor/body))))]))\n        caller (h/publish-guest-module!\n                 (module/module-spec :test/refusal :test/undeclared registry\n                                     {:name 'test.caller :ast caller-ast :exports '#{run}\n                                      :runtime-name 'clj :runtime-address (:address runtime)\n                                      :deps {'test.clj-donor (:address donor)}}))\n        source (link/composition\n                 {:content-store store :derivation :trusted\n                  :name-env {'clj (:address runtime) 'yang.call call-address\n                             'yrt.effect effect-address\n                             'test.clj-donor (:address donor) 'test.caller (:address caller)}})\n        program (u/sexp->uast '(do (require 'test.caller) (test.caller/run)))]\n    (is (contains? prelude/module-exports 'rt-ctx))\n    (is (some? (:address donor)) (pr-str donor))\n    (is (some? (:address caller)) (pr-str caller))\n    (is (not (contains? (core/free-names unit) 'clj.rt/ctx)))\n    (is (contains? (core/free-names unit) 'clj/run-unit))\n    (doseq [backend [:semantic :stack :register]]\n      (is (= 42 (vm/value (h/run-linked backend program {:modules registry :link-source source})))\n          (str backend)))))\n(ns yang.call.conformance\n  \"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\n   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\n   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\n\n   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\n   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\n   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\n   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`, `py/run-main`,\n   `clj/run-main`), reads each named export from the donor runtime's global\n   namespace, and projects it into the caller runtime's namespace under the\n   same name; then the caller source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own\n   entry. The composition is a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is\n   rewritten, no foreign `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is\n   inserted, and the projected value is the donor's own callable value\n   (identity survives).\n\n   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n\n   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\n   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\n   refused until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\n    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n    [yang.rt.effect :as effect]\n    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    [yang.core.names :as names]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\n    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\n    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn- publish-guest!\n  \"Publish guest module `spec` into the harness store, throwing immediately\n   with `result` in ex-data if publication is refused.\"\n  [spec]\n  (let [result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n    (when (= :refused (:status result))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"Guest module publication refused: \" (or (:reason result) (:status result)))\n                      result)))\n    result))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-php\n  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-py\n  \"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\n   `yang.call` revision.\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                   (:call-address @h/published)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-effect\n  (delay (publish-guest! (effect/module-spec (h/registry)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private published-clj\n  \"`clj` published beside `js`, `php` and `py`, over the same host registry\n   and `yang.call` revision.\"\n  (delay (publish-guest!\n           (clj-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n                                    (:call-address @h/published)\n                                    (:address @published-effect)))))\n\n\n(defn- parse-ok\n  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n  [parse source]\n  (let [pk (parse source)]\n    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n    pk))\n\n\n(defn- python-export-symbol\n  [export]\n  (symbol (str \"xlang.python.export.\" export)))\n\n\n(defn- python-unit\n  [packet exports]\n  (u/lam [py-lower/globals-sym py-lower/globals-fn-sym]\n         (u/seq-nodes\n           (concat (map (fn [export]\n                          (u/sexp->uast\n                            (list 'py/global-set py-lower/globals-sym\n                         (list 'py/module-dict\n                               (list 'py/modules-ref {:py/str \"__main__\"}))\n                         {:py/str export})),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               (list 'yin/def (list 'quote (python-export-symbol name)) value)),\n    :render py-render/output},\n   :clojure\n   {:runtime 'clj,\n    :address #(:address @published-clj),\n    :refusal [:yang.clojure/refusal :yang.clojure/undeclared-free],\n    :deps (fn [] {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published)}),\n    :parse clj-comp/read-forms,\n    :unit (fn [packet exports] (clj-comp/lower-unit packet exports)),\n    :run-main 'clj/run-main,\n    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'clj/global-get export)),\n    :project (fn [name value]\n               ;; The runtime global namespace is the one binding (as\n               ;; `js/define-global!` is for a JS caller): `lower-unit`\n               ;; reads each projected name through `clj/global-get`, so\n               ;; no task-store binding duplicates it. A caller top-level\n               ;; definition of the same name publishes after the\n               ;; projection and shadows it.\n               (list 'clj/define-global! name value)),\n    :render clj-comp/output}})\n\n\n(defn- profile\n  [frontend]\n  (or (get frontends frontend)\n      (throw (ex-info \"frontend not admitted\" {:frontend frontend}))))\n\n\n(defn- modules\n  \"The host registry, admitted by every runtime profile that checks it,\n   with the clojure guest library's host surface installed beside them.\n   Donor publication declares free names over this same registry, so a\n   clojure donor using the guest library (its `kind` and `portable`\n   hosts) publishes like it runs.\"\n  []\n  (clj-prelude/admit (php-prelude/admit (h/registry))))\n\n\n(defn- claims-call-sites?\n  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 call-site key anywhere.\"\n  [ast]\n  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n\n\n(defn publish-donor!\n  \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\"\n  ([frontend source]\n   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \"xlang.donor.\" (name frontend)))))\n  ([frontend source module]\n   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit deps]} (profile frontend)\n         [refusal-key reason] refusal\n         ast (let [raw (core-module/module-tree\n                         [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n                          (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))])]\n               (cond-> raw\n                 (claims-call-sites? raw) u/annotate-call-sites))\n         spec (core-module/module-spec\n                refusal-key reason (modules)\n                {:name module,\n                 :ast ast,\n                 :exports '#{body},\n                 :runtime-name runtime,\n                 :runtime-address (address),\n                 :deps (if deps (deps) {})})\n         result (publish-guest! spec)]\n     {:frontend frontend,\n      :module module,\n      :address (:address result),\n      :links (:links result)})))\n\n\n\n(def ^:private default-adapter-arity\n  \"The largest count an adapter admits for a native name with no declared\n   profile (`:native` given as a plain set).\"\n  4)\n\n\n(def ^:private adapter-variadic-cap\n  \"How far an adapter extends a `:variadic` profile arity: an adapter is a\n   finite dispatch, so an open-ended arity needs a stated bound.\"\n  8)\n\n\n(defn- native-name?\n  \"True when `sym` statically names a primitive or host-module export.\"\n  [env sym]\n  (when-let [conv (::convention env)]\n    (and (symbol? sym)\n         (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n         (not (contains? (::defined env) sym))\n         (or (some? (namespace sym))\n             (contains? (:native conv) sym)))))\n\n\n(defn- macro-call?\n  [env macro-env sym]\n  (and (symbol? sym)\n       (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n       (or (contains? macro-env sym)\n           (contains? (:macros (::convention env)) sym))))\n\n\n  \"Allocate a descriptor supplied by trusted UAST/profile code.\"\n  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n  (cond-> (u/app (u/v 'cell/new) descriptor-ast)\n    tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-call-descriptor\n  \"Publish a private argument-vector body through the clj entry boundary.\n   A named definition can also register its body for direct calls in its unit.\"\n  ([body-ast tail?] (compile-call-descriptor body-ast tail? nil))\n  ([body-ast tail? local-name]\n   (let [meta (cond-> {:clj/type :function}\n                (= 2 (count (:params body-ast))) (assoc :clj/tail-call? true))\n         constructor (if local-name\n                       (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_local) (u/lit local-name) (u/lit meta) body-ast)\n                       (u/app (u/v 'clj/make-callable) (u/lit meta) body-ast))]\n     (cond-> constructor\n       tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-av-fn\n  ordinary application; macro-env only stops the native defn lowering.\"\n  [form tail? env macro-env top?]\n  (cond\n    ;; Literals: constants self-evaluate; collections with dynamic elements\n    ;; lower to constructor calls so their elements evaluate like Clojure\n    (literal? form)\n    (if (constant-form? form)\n      (compile-literal form tail?)\n      (compile-constructed-collection form tail? env macro-env))\n    ;; The empty list is self-evaluating data, not an application\n    (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) (compile-literal form tail?)\n    ;; Variables (symbols)\n    (symbol? form) (if (native-name? env form)\n                     (if (outcomes? env)\n                       (compile-call-descriptor (compile-adapter form env false macro-env) tail?)\n                       (compile-adapter form env tail? macro-env))\n                     (compile-variable form tail?))\n    ;; Special forms and function application\n    (seq? form)\n    (let [[operator & operands] form]\n      (cond\n        ;; dao.stream.apply call: (dao.stream.apply/call :op/name arg1 arg2)\n        (= operator 'dao.stream.apply/call)\n        (let [[op & args] operands]\n          (compile-dao-stream-apply-call op args env tail? macro-env))\n        ;; Native defn fallback: used only when no defmacro defn is in scope\n        ;; and the form actually matches defn syntax.\n        (and (contains? #{'defn 'defn-} operator)\n             (not (contains? macro-env operator)))\n        (do (check-top-level! env top? operator)\n            (compile-defn operator operands env tail? macro-env))\n\n        ;; Special forms\n18:    [yrt.effect/handlers\n120:    [yrt.effect/handle\n177:    [yrt.effect/perform\n635:(def ^:private av-modules\n636:  (data/register-data-module\n637:    (module/register-cell-module\n1110:(def ^:private outcome-modules\n2445:        (module/register-cell-module)\n16:     the hosts' UTF-16 code units: `(data/str-length \\\"a😀\\\")` is 2 on\n568:(defn- canonical-entries [coll]\n572:    :else (wrong-type! 'canonical-entries 0 :map-or-set)))\n616:   ['canonical-entries [1] canonical-entries]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
