{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '114,165p' src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc\nrg -n '\"'^Testing|''^FAIL|''^ERROR|''^Ran |''^[0-9]+ failures|''^  actual: clojure'\"' /tmp/dw-p2prime-runtime2.log | cut -c1-205 | tail -70\nhead -n 13 test/resources/yang/clojure/cc4-replay-snapshots.edn\nrg -n '(:yin.module/name|defn retarget|module-entry).*' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | head -20\"","aggregated_output":";;\n;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a produced tree carries the\n;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\n;; from canonical rows and emits it into the frontend-metadata side table\n;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n;; The walk lives here, beside the other shared tree transforms, so every\n;; frontend's module trees finalize the same way; `yang.clojure` owns the\n;; contract's validation over canonical rows.\n\n(defn annotate-call-sites\n  \"The finished map AST `node` with `:yang/call-site 1` on every\n   `:application` node, at every depth the row grammar knows. Literal\n   payloads are data, never syntax, and are not walked. Marking is\n   idempotent and preserves node metadata and every other key, so\n   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\"\n  [node]\n  (let [tag (:type node)\n        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)]\n    (when-not slots\n      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\" {:type tag, :node node})))\n    (let [walked (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n                           (case kind\n                             :node (update n field annotate-call-sites)\n                             :nodes (update n field\n                                            (fn [children]\n                                              (mapv annotate-call-sites\n                                                    children)))\n                             n))\n                         node\n                         slots)]\n      (cond-> walked\n        (= :application tag) (assoc :yang/call-site 1)))))\n6:Testing d2-wedge-min-repro\n9:ERROR in (test-h31-wedge-min-repro) (d2_wedge_min_repro.clj:72)\n12:  actual: clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo: fixture no longer compiles\n61:Testing yang.clojure-test\n64:ERROR in (test-intra-unit-call-lowering-guards-and-budget) (observer.cljc:212)\n74:  actual: clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo: Guest instruction budget exhausted\n184:Testing yang.rt.effect-test\n186:ERROR in (clojure-runtime-parity) (engine.cljc:54)\n189:  actual: clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo: Module link refused: undeclared-free\n260:ERROR in (clojure-runtime-parity) (engine.cljc:54)\n263:  actual: clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo: Module link refused: undeclared-free\n334:ERROR in (clojure-runtime-parity) (engine.cljc:54)\n337:  actual: clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo: Module link refused: undeclared-free\n408:Ran 114 tests containing 1066 assertions.\n409:0 failures, 5 errors.\n;; The post-fix reference bundle (manifest c1-2, constructed-collections-v1\n;; re-pin per ruling 1795017757000): re-recorded on the JVM for all eight\n;; members after the constructed-collection operand-ordering fix; only the\n;; argument-vector and lower-unit members changed bytes. The pre-fix bundle\n;; is retained verbatim as cc4-replay-snapshots-prefix-c1-1.edn, and the r2\n;; defect evidence (cc4-replay-dart-divergences.edn, cc4-replay-jvm*.*) stays\n;; immutable.\n[{:id :native,\n  :root\n  :segment/blake3-0aac99defd315ce7623ecefc08106f31653bd138fb5ae3f1f1d466bd93893c70