ependently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled shadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) `yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\n16:- **2026-11-21 (r6 → r7 Clojure-First Default & Legacy Track, plus landed-DRY reconciliation):** Three owner directives. **(D10) Default-profile inversion:** for `yang.python` (and later `yang.typescript`/`yang.php`), the **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** runtime profile; the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist, oracle-parity-proven, at their current content addresses), with their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float deferred until legacy demand justifies it. **(Clojure-first roadmap):** the implementation order re-sequenced so the Clojure prelude family (`yrt.effect`/`yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers, unified trusted `clj`, `clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core` facade, `clj.py`, the python lowerer's descriptor parameterization) is built FIRST — the other-language native preludes are untouched by those slices (zero golden churn; defquoted consolidation and emitter standardization for py/ts/php defer to the legacy track). **(DRY-alignment reconciliation):** §5.2 admission checks home in `yang.core.prelude-admission` (3→5 publics, at bound) keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure emission; §8.2 names both the guest linker modules (`yrt.*`) and their host emitter namespaces (`src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`) and acknowledges the analyzer's 3 self-loop warnings (macro self-reference, no multi-node cycles); defquoted consolidation accounted against the public-surface ledger; §2 gains the tao-architecture second-axiom alignment (the semantics descriptor is stream-resident interpreter configuration; the provenance tuple names the interpreter).\n89:   - **Intentional intra-Clojure domain sharing:** By explicit architectural design, `clj`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core` execute *inside* the Clojure semantics and exception domain and therefore share `(clj/rt-ctx)` intentionally so Clojure `(throw ...)` / `(try ... (finally ...))` and Python-syntax `try` / `except` / `finally` unwind across `clj → clj.py → clj` nesting on one coherent handler stack while saving and restoring `(clj/rt-ctx)` at every `yrt.effect/try-value` and `finally` boundary.\n92:4. **No shared mutable state:** Each stateful profile allocates its own task-local cells once per task in its own idempotent `init!` under its own private namespace (`py.rt/*`, `js.rt/*`, `php.rt/*`, `clj.rt/*`, `clj.py.rt/*`, `clojure.core.rt/*`); `clojure.core.impl` is pure and stateless.\n97:   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (`clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER declare (`:yin.module/primitives`) or export (`:yin.module/exports`) provenance-door primitives directly.** (Transitive `:yin.module/footprint` unions are governed by `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.)\n98:   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal implementation modules such as `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`) (`§6.3`).\n109:| Layer 2c: Ambient & Standard Libraries (clojure.core, clojure.core.impl, …) |\n183:   - **`kind/namespace [x]`:** One `:pure` unary export backed by `namespace`, enabling deterministic symbol/keyword rendering in `clojure.core.impl`.\n306:2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\n307:3. **Provenance-door security exclusion (direct declarations, not transitive footprint):** Checks each non-trusted module's (`yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) **direct** `:yin.module/primitives` (refusing `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance`) and **direct** `:yin.module/exports` (refusing any `dsg__*` export on **every** module including trusted Layer-2b runtimes), while governing transitive `:yin.module/footprint` through `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.\n350:  {:module 'clojure.core.impl,  :address \"<blake3-address>\"}\n436: :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n471:2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:** Free source identifiers resolve in strict order: (1) lexical scope (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal`), (2) per-module globals (`:vars` in `globals-cell`), (3) unit-bound ambient resolver (`:ambient` in `globals-cell`, passed via `:unit/run-main`), failing with a guest `NameError` on miss.\n473:   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`, computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**, and inspects every active hook, executable `:literals.*` target, and `:ambient-projections` entry directly against the target manifest's verified `:yin.module/tree` UAST (`wide-app` top-level `(yin/def (quote sym) expr)` definitions):\n477:     - **Reserved-door ban:** refuses any reference to `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`).\n531:   - **Key/element admission:** Map/set construction and lookup in both `clj.py` and `clojure.core.impl` call `(data/admit-key? k)` once; on `false`, perform `:coll/unsupported-key` (raising `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` or `ex-info`).\n548:| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Invokes `clojure.core.impl/impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest` (backed by `data/canonical-entries` for maps/sets), raises guest error on non-collection iterables, and invokes `step-fn` per element. |\n558:- `clj` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters, never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core`.\n569:### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n573:1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\n585:   - Requires `clj` and `clojure.core.impl`. Exports only cell-free pure functions at install time: idempotent 0-arg `init!` (building `{sym cell}` with `clj/prim-assoc` and `clj/make-callable`), 1-arg `export` (using `clj/prim-get`), and 0-arg cell-accessor exports `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`.\n600:- `is_empty`, `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\n648:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store before VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py` exists. |\n670:   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):